Cross-host CXL fabric verification on g3 + g4
==============================================

Test binary: tests/cxl_xhost_test
Backing:     /dev/dax0.0 on each host
Date:        2026-04-21 ~03:00 CDT

Host 0 role: g3
Host 1 role: g4

=== g3 (host 0) output ===
[host 0] wrote payload + handshake; waiting for ACK...
[host 0] got ACK after 0.000s
OK: cross-host CXL fabric verified on /dev/dax0.0

=== g4 (host 1) output ===
[host 1] waiting for peer's handshake...
[host 1] saw handshake after 1.520s; verifying payload
[host 1] payload verified; ACK sent
OK: cross-host CXL fabric verified on /dev/dax0.0

Interpretation
--------------
- Handshake propagated g3 -> g4 in ~1.5 s (dominated by the start-up
  ordering and the 200 us spin cadence in the waiter; NOT an actual
  transport latency).
- 12 cachelines of distinct patterns verified byte-for-byte across
  hosts.
- Conclusion: /dev/dax0.0 on g3 and /dev/dax0.0 on g4 point at the
  same physical CXL memory through the PCIe switch / memory server.
  Good to run multi-host A/B/C benches on this testbed.
